# Synapse client config is per-machine (base_url, handle, channels for *this* user).
# The example templates (*.example.toml) ARE committed; copy them locally.
orchestrator/config/synapse.toml
orchestrator/config/project_hints.toml

# MindStone for Claude Code — user-specific orchestrator content
# Each developer's Cairn-like instance is private to them; the repo ships
# the framework (hooks, schema, templates, design docs) but NOT individual
# identity, user profile, session log, or accumulated personal memory.
# See orchestrator/memory/CAIRN_DESIGN_v0.3.md §8 (public/private boundary).
orchestrator/IDENTITY.md
orchestrator/USER.md
orchestrator/LOG.md
orchestrator/DOCS_UPDATED.md
orchestrator/memory/feedback_*.md
orchestrator/memory/project_*.md
orchestrator/memory/reference_*.md
orchestrator/memory/lineage_*.md
# The memory INDEX is private for the same reason the memories are. Every line in
# it summarises a gitignored file -- names, hosts, projects, people. Keeping the
# index on the public side of this boundary guarantees it drifts back across:
# it is written by the same /checkpoint flow that writes the private memories.
# Ships as onboarding/MEMORY.md.example instead, like IDENTITY/USER/AGENTS.
orchestrator/memory/MEMORY.md
# User-private skills (project-specific scripts referencing private infra,
# IPs, credentials, keys). Substrate-mechanic skills can be opted in by
# moving them out of skills/ into hooks/ or by carving a sub-path exception.
orchestrator/skills/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
# KEPT (framework-level, team/public-shareable):
#   orchestrator/memory/CAIRN_DESIGN_*.md   — design documentation
#   orchestrator/memory/.migrate_frontmatter.py — schema migration utility

# Wake-daemon config (per-machine; secret_file path is sensitive)
orchestrator/config/wake-daemon.toml
